# Git and IDE
**/.git
**/.github
**/.gitignore
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.classpath
**/.dockerignore
**/.toolstarget
**/.vs
**/.next
**/.cache
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm

# Dependencies (installed in container)
**/node_modules
**/.npm
**/npm-debug.log

# Build outputs (rebuilt in container)
**/build
**/dist
./frontend/dist
./frontend/dist/*

# Documentation and tests (not needed in production)
__docs/
tests/
test-results/
**/*.md
LICENSE
CONTRIBUTING.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Local development files
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.yml
!config/*.yml
!__backend/config/*.yml
# Authored Fitness course YAML must reach the image at its owner path.
# School Rubiks course data is compiled into courseSource.mjs and needs no YAML exception.
!__app_modules/wellness/fitness/server/adapters/courses/*.yml
# School's seed installer reads these examples from its owning module.
!__app_modules/learning/school/seeds/**/*.yml
secrets.dev.yaml
values.dev.yaml
**/charts
**/docker-compose*
# Compose's modern filenames only. This used to be `**/compose*`, which is a
# prefix glob over EVERY path segment, not just compose files: it silently
# dropped `composerCardTiming.js` out of the build context while leaving
# `ComposerCard.jsx` (capital C) in, so the image failed to build on an import
# that resolves fine in the repo. Any lowercase compose-prefixed source file
# would hit the same trap.
**/compose.yml
**/compose.yaml
**/compose.*.yml
**/compose.*.yaml
**/obj

# Data and logs (mounted at runtime)
_deleteme/
.pii-scrub/
.firecrawl/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
./data
./data/*
logs/
*.log

# Dev tools
scripts/config/

# Extensions (separate build)
_extensions/
_extentions/
